WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.280
"Game of Thrones" was notorious for its&nbsp;
unflinching depictions of violence, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.400
"House of the Dragon" follows suit. In the first&nbsp;
episode, Prince Daemon's Gold Cloaks try to rid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:16.160
King's Landing of its criminal element by using&nbsp;
extrajudicial torture and death as a deterrent.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.400
Daemon's men cut off hands&nbsp;
and do much worse. This…

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.800
"...public spectacle of wanton brutality…"

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.280
…wasn't just dreamt up by show creators;&nbsp;
they're the precise punishments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.160
doled out by Daemon and his Gold Cloaks in&nbsp;
author George R.R. Martin's "Fire &amp; Blood."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.360
In the book and, it seems, the series,&nbsp;
Daemon's brand of justice makes him popular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.560
thanks to claims that he's making the city safer.

